// REJECTS: Unexpected token '{'. Valid alternatives: ['=', ';']
//
// Tagged values and stereotypes are a PREFIX on a property: `{profile.tag = 'v'} code:
// String[1];`. This puts the tagged value where a trailing annotation would naturally go,
// after the type and multiplicity.
//
// The alternatives are the tell: having read `String[1]` the parser will accept '=' (a
// default value) or ';'. So the position is not merely unconventional, it collides with a
// real construct -- which means a rewrite that also accepts a trailing annotation block
// has quietly created an ambiguity it will have to resolve by guessing.
###Pure
Class fixture::neg::TagAfterMultiplicity
{
   code: String[1] {meta::pure::profiles::doc.doc = 'trailing tagged value'};
}
